---
description: Spec and task file conventions
globs: ["specs/**", "tasks/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# Specs (`specs/`)

- One spec per module at `specs/modules/<name>.md`; product-level specs at `specs/`.
- Use the template in `specs/README.md`: Purpose · Requirement refs · Public interface
  (capabilities, events, API routes) · Data owned · Behavior · Acceptance criteria ·
  Out of scope.
- Every spec cites the build-doc sections it derives from
  (`docs/TenderShield_Full_Build_Doc.md`). Anything beyond the doc is marked
  `assumption:`.
- Specs and code must never contradict; fix the mismatch in the same change.

# Tasks (`tasks/backlog.md`)

- IDs are sequential `TS-###`, never reused.
- Fields: ID, title, phase (P0/P1/…), requirement ref, spec ref, status, notes.
- Statuses: `todo | in-progress | blocked | done`.
- Order the backlog by build value (Build Doc §13.5): risk patterns → BOQ engine →
  clarification letter → billing. Don't pull Phase-2+ tasks before Phase-1 gates pass.
